./chapters/01-cell-file.html:30:<p>The unit is one bounded robot cell. The initial product is a fixed-scope <em>cell-file challenge</em>: review the integrator's risk assessment, inspect the installed cell, witness agreed safety-function tests, execute the agreed force-and-pressure test plan, and issue a signed findings report. The customer receives a technical-file index, evidence gaps and a draft validation record. The integrator closes the gaps, owns the design and signs its declaration.</p>
./chapters/01-cell-file.html:63:<p>The online record does not settle the pitch's kill fact. IAB publishes €6,000 for CE work on a simple machine and about €30,000 for a machinery assembly, both including a manual. <!-- CHECK: 01-incumbent-price --> Those are broad anchors, not cobot-cell quotes. The named Dutch integrator and safety-bureau pages reviewed here publish scope but no cell-file price. <!-- CHECK: 01-price-boundary --> The record therefore cannot exclude a dealer bundling the work or a competent bureau quoting below €3,000.</p>
./chapters/04-spray-crew-file.html:30:<p>The unit is one crew doing one defined process under one set of controls. The fixed-scope <em>spray-crew baseline</em> inventories products and safety data sheets, maps tasks and workers, audits training evidence, observes a normal job, and produces a quantitative exposure assessment. The Dutch-speaking occupational hygienist chooses and reviews the method. If a model cannot close the question, the file specifies representative measurements and records the results.</p>
./checks/claims/01.tsv:20:01-price-boundary	The named Dutch integrator and machinery-safety pages reviewed publish service scope but no comparable cobot-cell file price; this does not exclude unpublished quotes below €3,000.	https://www.pilz.com/nl-NL/services/machinery-safety	research inference across Pilz, Yaskawa, D-SC, Olmia and IAB pages; no excerpt	inference
./chapters/02-border-files.html:65:<p>The kill fact is only partly settled. Customs Support Group markets customs clearance beside CBAM and EUDR reporting, with more than 1,700 customs experts and 60,000 clients. <!-- CHECK: 02-customs-support --> Deloitte Netherlands markets an integrated service spanning supplier solicitation, validation, authorised declaration and customs brokerage. <!-- CHECK: 02-deloitte-incumbent --> These firms can bundle the work. Neither publishes a comparable small-importer price or says the supplier-data work is free. <!-- CHECK: 02-price-boundary --> Two live broker quotes are still required.</p>
./resources/sources/01/SOURCES.md:68:    Supports: the incumbent's marketed lifecycle from assessment through integration, validation and conformity work (`01-pilz-competition`). Also one input to the unpublished-price inference (`01-price-boundary`).
