./research/pitch-02/index.html:27:<p><strong>The kill fact.</strong> A dealer or safety body already sells the cell file to SMEs under €3,000, or Dutch SME technical staff will not buy it in English. The review found dealers doing risk analysis in-house (Olmia) and one SME using an external expert (Automise, 2021), so the market exists; the price is the open question. Call two dealers.</p>
./research/ideation-assembled-machines/index.html:51:<ol><li>Does Regulation 2023/1230 apply from 20 Jan 2027, and does Art. 3/10 make the assembler the manufacturer? (EUR-Lex PDF via curl.)</li><li>Is EN ISO 10218-2:2025 published and cited in the OJ under the Regulation, and by when? (ISO catalogue; OJ C series harmonised-standards list.)</li><li>How many industrial robots and cobots were installed in NL in 2024 and 2025? (IFR World Robotics 2025 country table; the search gave Europe 85,000, cobots ~12%, no NL figure.)</li><li>Do UR, Doosan or Fanuc Dutch distributors bundle the cell CE with installation, at what price? (Distributor sites; two phone calls.)</li><li>What do D-SC, Fusacon, Pilz NL, Perios and Olmia charge per cobot cell today? (Their sites; Olmia whitepaper in sources.)</li><li>Does the Dutch Labour Inspectorate treat an integrated cobot as a new machine under Arbobesluit art. 7.2–7.4? (Arboportaal; NLA inspection reports.)</li><li>What does an ISO/TS 15066 force-measurement set cost to buy or rent? (Pilz PRMS/GTE, Schmersal, rental firms.)</li><li>How many Polish integrators sell cells into NL, and do their Dutch customers ask for the file? (Polish robotics association member lists; UR partner map.)</li><li>Can a one-person Dutch firm get professional liability cover for signing CE files, and at what premium? (Two Dutch brokers.)</li><li>Under the Regulation, must the manufacturer sign the declaration, so the reader's file is always countersigned by the integrator? (Art. 10 and Annex V.)</li><li>How many Dutch pack-houses and food SMEs automated in 2024–25 (subsidy lists, VNO-NCW/FME surveys)?</li></ol>
./research/ideation-assembled-machines/index.html:61:<ol><li>Exact wording of Art. 3 "substantial modification" and Art. 18 in 2023/1230. (EUR-Lex PDF.)</li><li>Does Directive 2024/2853 Art. 8 treat a substantial modifier as manufacturer, transposition 9 Dec 2026? (EUR-Lex.)</li><li>Has the Commission published Machinery Regulation guidance on which retrofits are substantial? (DG GROW machinery page; the 2006/42 Guide §72 as baseline.)</li><li>How many NLA inspection cases in 2023–25 concerned modified machines? (Nederlandse Arbeidsinspectie annual reports.)</li><li>What share of Dutch SME machine parks is pre-CE (before 1995) or pre-2010? (FME or Metaalunie surveys; CBS capital-stock age.)</li><li>How many Polish retrofit and controls shops serve Dutch customers? (Polish automation association; LinkedIn.)</li><li>What do Dutch bureaus charge for a modification assessment? (IAB, D-SC, Perios price pages.)</li><li>Is the used-machinery trade (a border question, sibling seed) already shipping "CE packages" with retrofits, undercutting the memo? (Polish dealer sites.)</li><li>Do Dutch insurers require a modification assessment after retrofit? (Insurer machine-breakdown conditions.)</li><li>Does the employer duty in Arbobesluit art. 7.4a require an inspection after modification, by whom? (Arboportaal.)</li></ol>
./research/ideation-assembled-machines/sources/search-ce-robotcel.txt:9:- https://d-sc.nl/cobots-functionaliteit-en-veiligheid/
./research/ideation-assembled-machines/sources/search-ce-robotcel.txt:11:- https://www.olmia-robotics.nl/files/whitepaper/OR_RisicoanalyseCobotcel.pdf
./research/ideation-assembled-machines-reviewed/index.html:33:<ol><li><strong>Iron plus paper.</strong> A cobot cell, palletiser, AMR fleet or packing line assembled from CE-marked parts is a new machine; whoever installs it owes risk assessment, technical file and declaration. <em>(Shape verified by two integrators' own pages: Olympus "the integrator is normally the manufacturer"; Nooteboom case delivered "CE-markering voor het samenstel".)</em></li><li><strong>Dated rule.</strong> 20 Jan 2027, Regulation 2023/1230 <strong>(verified)</strong>; EN ISO 10218-2:2025 published, OJ citation pending <strong>(partly verified)</strong>.</li><li><strong>Buyers.</strong> SME manufacturers of 10–100 staff and small integrators, Polish ones included. Incumbents €6,000 per machine, €30,000 per assembly <strong>(verified)</strong>.</li><li><strong>Edge.</strong> Reads the Regulation; a templated evidence trail with measured force and stopping distance; Polish integrator channel. No Dutch exam <strong>(the UK precedent's only credential is a private "Certified Machinery Safety Expert" badge, not a state exam)</strong>.</li><li><strong>Per unit.</strong> €1,500–3,000 per cell, €4–8k per line <strong>(estimate)</strong>; first test three cells for one integrator ≈ €4,500; measuring set €5–10k <strong>(estimate)</strong>. Step two: Dutch safety engineer. Step three: see addition E.</li><li><strong>AI.</strong> Every cheaper cobot is one more assembly; the force measurement is a person with a meter at the cell.</li><li><strong>Kill fact.</strong> A distributor bundles the cell file free, or a bureau sells it at ≤€1,500. <strong>Not triggered by what was found</strong>: Olmia does the risk analysis "samen met jou" and does not advertise a CE file; Automise had its RI&amp;E "beoordeeld door een extern deskundige".</li><li><strong>Precedent — found.</strong> <em>Cobots and Machinery Safety Ltd</em>, Corby, UK: one engineer (Matt Androsiuk), incorporated 10 July 2019, company 12096383, active; sells "Cobot Risk Assessments", "Cobot Force and Pressure Testing", "UKCA and CE Marking", light-curtain testing and EN ISO 10218-2 training to "UK manufacturers"; no prices published. Second, older: <em>Machine Safety Specialists</em>, Ohio, "since 1977", industrial and collaborative robot safety assessments and validation to ANSI/RIA and ISO standards. Third-tier: <em>CE-CON GmbH</em>, Bremen, 20+ years, but half software. (<code>precedent-A-*.txt</code>)</li></ol>
./research/ideation-assembled-machines-reviewed/index.html:58:<p><strong>Do Dutch cobot dealers subcontract CE today?</strong> Two data points, no survey: Olmia (Tiel) does the risk analysis "samen met jou" and does not advertise CE; Automise wrote Nooteboom's RI&amp;E with the customer's safety officer and had it "beoordeeld door een extern deskundige" (MetaalNieuws, 2021). So dealers do the analysis in-house and, at least sometimes, buy an external review. The external review is A's slot; E is what A grows into. Verdict: not an entry, a step three. (<code>addition-*.txt</code>)</p>
./research/ideation-assembled-machines-reviewed/index.html:64:<p>1 Commission machinery page · 2 Commission batteries page · 3 Commission PLD page · 4 FLI AI Act timeline · 5 ce-con.de · 6 laidler.co.uk (failed, TLS) · 7 machinesafetyspecialists.com · 8 batterieingenieure.de · 9 robotobor.nl · 10 search: cobot integrator CE · 11 cobotsmachinerysafety.co.uk · 12 Olympus CE guide · 13 Olympus palletiser cost · 14 search: Dutch dealers CE · 15 search: battery dates · 16 search: Poland minimum requirements · 17 search: battery consultancy · 18 search: ML safety functions · 19 Companies House · 20 MetaalNieuws Nooteboom · 21 Olmia diensten · 22 farempoland.pl · 23 300gospodarka · 24 conformance.co.uk · 25 search: ISO 10218-2. Not fetched: EUR-Lex (any form), NL robot counts, a Polish per-machine price, an independent trace for Farem or Olympus.</p>
